{
"dur": 38.14,
"shots": [
{
"i": 1,
"start": 0.0,
"vo_start": 0.6,
"vo_end": 5.88,
"text": "On the twenty-third of February 1981, armed police burst into Spain's parliament during a live vote.",
"end": 6.155
},
{
"i": 2,
"start": 6.155,
"vo_start": 6.43,
"vo_end": 13.301,
"text": "Their leader climbed onto the speaker's platform with a pistol and fired at the ceiling. Most of the deputies dived under their seats.",
"end": 13.576
},
{
"i": 3,
"start": 13.576,
"vo_start": 13.851,
"vo_end": 22.931,
"text": "Spain had been a democracy for less than four years. For the thirty-six years before that, it had been ruled by one general. Now the army was trying to bring those days back.",
"end": 23.206
},
{
"i": 4,
"start": 23.206,
"vo_start": 23.481,
"vo_end": 30.92,
"text": "That night, at about one in the morning, the king appeared on television in his army uniform. And what he said decided the fate of the country.",
"end": 31.195
},
{
"i": 5,
"start": 31.195,
"vo_start": 31.47,
"vo_end": 37.19,
"text": "To understand that night, you have to go back to a war that killed hundreds of thousands of Spaniards, and the general who won it.",
"end": 38.14
}
],
